      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 2004 Wiley-Liss, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "Phrenic nerve paralysis is a condition typically occurring after invasive procedures in the chest and neck. Here we describe a case of transient unilateral diaphragmatic paralysis in a child with status asthmaticus complicated by complete right lung atelectasis. Common causes of this disorder and possible implications for our case are discussed."
      },
